WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar. Four circles of equal size are inscribed in a square.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:11.729
Inside of the four circles is a smaller square tangent to each of the four circles.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:18.390
If the large square has a side length equal to four, what is the area of the small square?

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:26.098
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution.

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:35.909
The first thing we'll do is: we'll consider the centers of each circle.

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:40.229
Now, we'll solve for the radius of a single circle.

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:48.239
If, we extend the radius across two adjacent circles, we'll see that it spans the side of the large square

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:58.050
The large square side is equal to four times the length of the radius of a single circle, and this is equal to four.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:03.029
So, we can solve that each circle has a radius r equals one.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.890
Now, let's form a triangle between the centers of three circles.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:18.849
This will be an isosceles right triangle, where each leg is equal to two.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:28.000
The hypotenuse of this isosceles right triangle will be two times the square root of two (2*√2). You can solve for this by the Pythagorean theorem.

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:34.419
But, we can also solve for the length of the hypotenuse by considering the distances involved.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.570
We have one radius length.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:43.720
Then, we have the length of the small square, which we'll denote by x, and then we have another radius length.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:48.429
So, we now have two different ways to measure the hypotenuse.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:56.600
On the one hand, it's equal to two square root of two, and on the other hand, it's equal to two plus x, where x is the small square side length.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:02.080
We can therefore solve that x is equal to 2 square root of two minus two.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:07.539
This means the area of the small square is the square of x which equals

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:11.229
twelve minus eight square root of two and that's approximately

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.400
point six eight six.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.540
Did you figure it out?

